{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses came and told the people all the words of YHWH.</b> The command of separation and boundary-setting; and 'all the judgments' — one should not explain these as the civil laws in the section 'And these are the judgments,' for it has already been clarified that this passage was before the giving of the Torah, but rather the judgments here are Sabbath and civil laws and the red heifer, which they were commanded at Marah."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:26.198758947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}